*** Kender who manage to gain 17 Strength can reach 6th level.**

Surprise: Due to their watchfulness, kender penalize opponent's surprise roll by -4.

Fearlessness: Kender are immune to both natural and magical fear. Still, kender are not stupid and will recognize danger quickly. Their reaction will tend toward fascination and curiosity, not fear.

Taunting: Kender can taunt others into reckless acts. Their taunting tone is so annoying that enemies may become enraged. If enemies fail a save vs. spell, they act with mindless rage for 1d10 rounds and suffer a penalty of 2 to THAC0, Armor Class, and all action rolls.

## Thieving Skills

Tales of the Lance:

Even kender who are not handlers have an inherent ability to perform as a low-level thief:
- Pick Pockets 25%;
- Open Locks 25%;
- Find/Remove Traps 25%;
- Move Silently 25%;
- Hide in Shadows 25%;
- Detect Noise 25%;
- Climb Walls 50%;
- Read Languages 10%.

Dragonlance Appendix:

Kender who are not thieves have a base 5% chance to perform any thieving skill except reading languages (no chance) and climbing (base 40% chance); these chances never improve except for Dexterity and racial modifiers (kender are treated as halflings with regard to climbing)

Bronze Half-Dragon is the product of a male Bronze Dragon and a female human/demihuman. Possible demihumans include elves, half-elves, dwarves, gnomes, halflings, kender, and similar humanlike races (including drow).

Cannot multiclass or dual-class. One class only.

Can exceed the level limits for the allowable classes if they have high prime requisite scores (DMG Table 8).

Can choose to use any kit allowed to its class and to its human/demihuman parent's race, except the "dragon-rider" kit and any kit involving the slaying or harming of dragons. There are 2 new kits for just Half-Dragon PCs: Exile Kit & Ward Kit. Can choose not to use a kit at all.

## Racial Abilities

Half-Dragons appear more draconic in features, until they reach full maturity at 7th level.

## Human Mother

Characters starts with no racial abilities.
- Even-Numbered levels: the player chooses a Discretionary Ability to gain, until the list is exhausted (or reach level-cap).
- 5th level: gain the ability to use their talonlike nails as claw weapons. (fixed ability)
- 7th level: Unlocks the half-dragon breath weapon. (fixed ability)

## Demihuman Mother

Characters start at level 1 with all the racial abilities of their demihuman parent
- 2nd, 4th, and 6th levels: Choose a Discretionary Ability to replace one of their demi-human racial abilities.
  - The DM can choose what ability is lost, or leave it up to the player.
- 5th level: gain the ability to use their talonlike nails as claw weapons. (fixed ability)
- 7th level: Unlocks the half-dragon breath weapon. (fixed ability)

## Abilities List

## Discretionary abilities

- Water breathing (at will);
- speak with animals (at will);
- create food and water (twice per day);
- ESP (once per day);
- dragon fear (once per day);
- immune to electricity;
- 60′ infravision

## Fixed abilities

- Claw Attacks (1d6/1d6)
- Breath Weapon (bolt of lightning 8' long damage 3d4, usable twice per day)

## Thieving Skills

- Pick Pockets +5%;
- Open Locks +0%;
- Find/Remove Traps -5%;
- Move Silently +10%;
- Hide in Shadows +10%;
- Detect Noise +0%;
- Climb Walls +0%;
- Read Languages +0%.

